        "answer": {
          "short": "$E(X)=7.01$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)\\approx7.49$, $\\sigma\\approx2.74$.",
          "worked": "Enter the outcomes in the $x$ column and their probabilities in the frequency column. Use the population statistics from 1-variable results.\n$$\\begin{align*}E(X)&=\\bar{x}=7.01\\\\\\operatorname{Var}(X)&=\\sigma_x^2=7.4899\\approx7.49\\\\\\sigma&=\\sqrt{7.4899}\\approx2.74\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$P(x)=\\dfrac{x+1}{9}$ for $x\\in\\{0,2,4\\}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$E(X)\\approx2.89$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)\\approx1.88$, $\\sigma\\approx1.37$.",
          "worked": "$$P(0)=\\frac19,\\qquad P(2)=\\frac13,\\qquad P(4)=\\frac59.$$ Enter $0,2,4$ in the $x$ column and these probabilities in the frequency column. Use the population statistics from 1-variable results.\n$$\\begin{align*}E(X)&=\\bar{x}=\\frac{26}{9}\\approx2.89\\\\\\operatorname{Var}(X)&=\\sigma_x^2=\\frac{152}{81}\\approx1.88\\\\\\sigma&=\\frac{\\sqrt{152}}9\\approx1.37\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
