        "answer": {
          "short": "$P(5)=\\dfrac3{10}$; $E(X)=2.75$, $\\operatorname{Var}(X)\\approx2.89$, $\\sigma\\approx1.70$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}P(5)&=1-\\left(\\frac25+\\frac1{10}+\\frac3{20}+\\frac1{20}\\right)\\\\P(5)&=\\frac3{10}\\end{align*}$$ Enter $1,2,3,4,5$ in the $x$ column and $\\frac25,\\frac1{10},\\frac3{20},\\frac1{20},\\frac3{10}$ in the frequency column. Use the population statistics from 1-variable results.\n$$\\begin{align*}E(X)&=\\bar{x}=2.75\\\\\\operatorname{Var}(X)&=\\sigma_x^2=2.8875\\approx2.89\\\\\\sigma&=\\sqrt{2.8875}\\approx1.70\\end{align*}$$",
